Yes. Hermes makes this architecture cleaner because it gives us a ready-made **agent execution + skills + delegation + automation substrate** rather than forcing the Media OS to invent its own agent runtime. Hermes already has persistent skills, skill bundles, subagents, MCP, plugins, webhooks, cron, a local management dashboard and REST endpoints for managing parts of its configuration. ([Hermes Agent][1])

The key architectural decision I would make is:

> **Media OS owns truth, state, assets, pipelines, analytics and scheduling of production. Hermes owns intelligent work. Postiz owns social I/O.**

That separation lets practically anything that can output an MP4 + manifest plug into the network.

