# 1. Make MP4 + JSON the universal input contract

This is the biggest unlock.

Anything that creates media should be capable of handing us:

```text
video.mp4
manifest.json
```

It doesn't matter whether that MP4 came from:

* your rendering engine
* LTX
* Remotion
* Blender
* FFmpeg
* another AI agent
* a human editor
* an uploaded stock video
* some future video model

The Media OS accepts it.

I'd define a **Media Package**.

```json
{
  "schema": "media.package/v1",

  "content_id": "prehistoric-000042",
  "brand": "prehistoric",

  "asset": {
    "type": "video",
    "uri": "file:///output/raptor-42.mp4",
    "sha256": "...",
    "duration_seconds": 44.18,
    "aspect_ratio": "9:16"
  },

  "content": {
    "subject": "velociraptor",
    "concept": "pack hunting",
    "title": "The Raptor Hunt",
    "language": "en"
  },

  "features": {
    "hook": "misconception",
    "structure": "hunt",
    "opening": "immediate-reveal",
    "setting": "night",
    "mechanisms": [
      "pov",
      "size-comparison",
      "swarm"
    ]
  },

  "targets": [
    "youtube_shorts",
