# 7. And make a Hermes Media OS plugin

There's another layer that's even nicer.

Hermes explicitly recommends **plugins** for custom integrations involving authentication, precise processing, binary data or streaming, while skills are more appropriate for procedural instructions built from existing tools. ([Hermes Agent][4])

So I'd build:

```text
hermes-media-os/
├── plugin.yaml
├── __init__.py
├── schemas.py
├── tools.py
└── skills/
```

And expose clean tools:

```text
media_claim_job
media_get_content
media_get_asset
media_submit_artifact

media_query_metrics
media_create_experiment

media_request_render
media_request_publish
```

Hermes plugins can register tools, hooks, commands, CLI commands and bundled skills without modifying Hermes core. ([Hermes Agent][4])

This is exactly what we want.

