## The key boundaries

**Postgres**
= truth.

**R2/MinIO**
= artifact memory.

**Temporal**
= durable state/time/retries.

**Hermes**
= intelligence/workforce.

**Hermes skills**
= procedural memory.

**Hermes cron**
= recurring cognitive routines.

**MCP/plugin**
= Hermes ↔ Media OS bridge.

**Postiz**
= distribution/auth/social provider abstraction.

**Langfuse**
= agent observability.

**Control UI**
= your cockpit.

And **MP4 + manifest** is the contract that lets the rest of the ecosystem attach itself.

The most valuable part may ultimately not even be the dashboard. It may be the underlying **media execution protocol**: any model, renderer, editor or agent can submit a structured artifact; the system knows what it is, where it came from, what should happen to it, which agents/skills are permitted to touch it, when it should publish, and how its eventual performance feeds back into the system that produced it. That turns the project from “automated YouTube channels” into a reusable infrastructure layer for running autonomous media networks.

